{#- formulas/openbao-snapshot — pulls a Raft snapshot of OpenBao over its API
   onto this host (salt-master), where formulas/backup picks it up. OpenBao
   itself (.20) is not a minion; this only needs an AppRole that may read
   sys/storage/raft/snapshot and nothing else (README "Bootstrap").

   addr: OpenBao's API URL. ca_file: CA that signed its TLS cert (on the
   master: the one formulas/salt-master already uses for sdb).
   role_id: not secret (like salt-master:lookup:vault_role_id).
   secret_id_file: placed by hand (security-critical bootstrap), root-only,
   no trailing newline. The state only checks that it exists.

   target_dir/file: the snapshot is written as <file>.tmp and renamed, so a
   failed run leaves the last good one. Keep target_dir inside the
   minion's backup paths (pillar/backup.sls).

   on_calendar: before formulas/backup's 02:00 run, so the nightly restic
   snapshot carries a fresh one. Persistent: a missed night runs at boot.

   textfile_dir: node-exporter's textfile collector (metrics
   openbao_snapshot_*; alerts in pillar/prometheus.sls).
   ping_slug: Healthchecks check <slug>-<minion id> while
   formulas/healthchecks-ping has a ping key. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'addr': '',
    'ca_file': '/etc/salt/pki/master/openbao-ca.pem',
    'role_id': '',
    'approle_mount': 'approle',
    'config_dir': '/etc/openbao-snapshot',
    'secret_id_file': '/etc/openbao-snapshot/secret-id',
    'target_dir': '/var/backups/openbao',
    'file': 'openbao.snap',
    'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    'script': '/usr/local/sbin/openbao-snapshot',
    'unit': 'openbao-snapshot',
    'on_calendar': '*-*-* 01:30:00 Europe/Berlin',
    'randomized_delay': '5min',
    'timeout': '10min',
    'http_timeout': 120,
    'textfile_dir': '/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter',
    'ping_slug': 'openbao-snapshot',
} %}
{%- set openbao_snapshot = salt['pillar.get']('openbao_snapshot:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
